's value — of an engine and of an outside-target span too — is held in process memory until the span closes and written only where the rule prints it; an event's line is unchanged, inside a span included. A named limit, read from the locked `tracing-subscriber 0.3.23` and not exercised: when a field formatter returns an error at span creation the layer itself `eprintln!`s the span's attributes with `Debug` to stderr, unscrubbed — the sink's field formatter writes into a `String` and returns no error (packages/escher-telemetry/src/lib.rs:102-116; packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:138-177; packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:200-250; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md). Its reach is that sink only: the upstream apps' `fmt::init()` stdout subscribers and the WPT runner's `env_logger` stay unscrubbed, the chained std panic hook still prints the raw panic message to stderr, and an allowlisted `log.file` can still carry a host path, now only for a bridged record under an engine target — the bridged third-party records that carried one at `RUST_LOG=info` (as measured at the chunk's smoke, escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-telemetry-bootstrap/report.md) are dropped whole (recorded by construction, not measured: a dropped record writes zero bytes, and `log.file` occurrences were not counted). Since 2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist no record from a target outside the allowlist reaches stderr — stderr lines before → after the drop: the `escher-session` binary (the CRUD task, one `hello`, then `stop`) 0 → 0 at the default level, 1 → 1 at `info`, 1165 → 1 at `debug`, 1501 → 1 at `trace`; the windowed `seven_guis_native` (left on Home for 10 s, nobody clicks) 1 → 0, 3 → 1, 12,413 → 1, 47,482 → 1 — the one line left being the install line `INFO escher_telemetry`, with no stable id and no accessible name at any setting on either binary and stdout empty in all 16 readings; the cost is that a third-party WARN or ERROR no longer prints either — the windowed stand's one default-level line, `WARN winit_wayland::window::state`, is gone; typed text was first measured in process: `stand_act_spans` re-runs its test binary on two ignored children, each installing the sink with `init_with_writer` over an in-memory capture, and at `RUST_LOG=info` the capture of the six instance-level verbs and a refused call for each of the eight causes holds 0 occurrences of the three supplied texts (the typed text, the id naming no element, the unknown verb's text), 0 of 36 id needles and 0 of 8 name needles, in both layout modes; typed text in a sink-installing HOST's log is measured since 2026-10-10-driver-cli — the `escher-session` host runs the calls its socket's `call` request carries and writes one closed `command` span line per call run (`host_log`: 3 lines for 3 calls), and a typed sentinel occurs 0 times in that host's stderr at `RUST_LOG=trace`, with 0 id needles and 0 name needles, under both builds (`host_log` as `-p seven_guis` and as `--workspace`); by level, on a snapshot · click · type flow, the host built alone writes 0 lines unset and 4 at `info`, `debug` and `trace` (three command spans and the install line), and the workspace-built host one engine line more, `blitz_dom::document` at INFO, with 0 sentinel occurrences, 0 of 15 ids and 0 of 6 names at every level and stdout 0 B (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/evidence/by-level.md); since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the sink also prints a second `escher_driver` span, `tool_call`, one closed line per MCP `tools/call`, holding `tool` (the table's word, absent for an unknown tool) and `ending` (`accepted` · `refused` · `error`) only, the parent of `command` — neither field in `CONTENT_FIELDS`, both closed words (answered by the founder, 2026-10-10, «Span с tool и ending», relayed by the overseer; packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:537-540) — and the `escher-session mcp` role's stderr over one CRUD flow at `info` reads 9 lines built alone and 10 built with the workspace (5 `tool_call` and 3 `command` in each), with 0 typed-sentinel occurrences, 0 id needles and 0 name needles at `trace` under both builds (`mcp_log`, examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:48-266; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-mcp-surface/report.md); since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot the verb table holds seven instance-level verbs and nine causes, `stand_act_spans` also reads a refused shot's line, `cause=fonts-unavailable`, and a shot's image reaches no log — the command span never records the image, its size or its dimensions, and the first 64 base64 characters of a shot occur 0 times in the `escher-session` host's and the `mcp` role's stderr at `RUST_LOG=trace`, under both builds (`host_log`, `mcp_log`; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:158-171; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-headless-screenshot/report.md); `seven_guis_native` still runs no command; the session host's by-level reading above, of a host that runs no call, was re-measured unchanged at 2026-10-07-driver-command-spans (0 · 1 · 1 · 1 stderr lines, 0 of 15 ids, 0 of 6 names, stdout 0 B), the windowed stand's read at `info` only, by its boot smoke, one line (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/evidence/by-level.md, the in-process capture and the re-measurement at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md)
